{
  "configuration_id": "config_012",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_038 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250 accuracy. All four aggregation×fusion combinations with scvi_n200+imagenet_vit_l+multiprofile have been tested, and scgpt and singleprofile are clearly inferior. The only untested RNA encoder in the optimal architecture is pca_n2000. This experiment tests whether pca_n2000 with the best-performing architecture (transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, imagenet_vit_l) can match or exceed scvi_n200, or confirm that scvi_n200 is the dominant RNA encoder. While scgpt underperformed, pca is a different (simpler, linear) method and its performance is genuinely uncertain. As the final experiment, this provides the most informative remaining data point about the RNA encoder axis while using the already-validated optimal architecture. Expected cost: moderate (~3–4 GPU hours), comparable to config_038 (3.60 hrs) since the architecture is identical and PCA encoding is slightly cheaper than scVI, keeping total budget reasonable."
}

